From 2eed580ada123c88dcb9670edc209e6c7834d12f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 15 Apr 2025 22:23:42 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Support additional HTTP headers for HTTP playback

Like the cookies stored on a media, the headers stored with
libvlc_media_header_jar_store() are replayed into a jar owned by the
player when libvlc_media_player_play() is called. The http access and
the adaptive demuxer inherit that jar through the "http-headers"
variable. The player jar is cleared on each play so the headers of a
media are not sent for the next one.
---
